WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.079
Words in Context

00:00:02.459 --> 00:00:04.658
Predict your own word before you look.

00:00:05.858 --> 00:00:06.949
How to spot it

00:00:07.349 --> 00:00:09.296
A blank or an underlined word

00:00:09.847 --> 00:00:11.522
Four single-word choices

00:00:12.072 --> 00:00:15.849
It’s testing: the precise meaning the context needs

00:00:17.049 --> 00:00:17.815
The method

00:00:18.215 --> 00:00:20.311
Step 1: Read the whole passage

00:00:20.591 --> 00:00:22.748
Not just the sentence with the blank.

00:00:23.298 --> 00:00:25.015
Step 2: Find the clue

00:00:25.295 --> 00:00:29.543
“But” and “although” flip the meaning. Colons and “because” match it.

00:00:30.093 --> 00:00:32.911
Step 3: Predict a simple word

00:00:33.191 --> 00:00:34.722
Say it in plain English.

00:00:35.272 --> 00:00:36.672
Step 4: Match it

00:00:36.952 --> 00:00:39.616
Check positive or negative, and how strong.

00:00:40.166 --> 00:00:41.261
In a few words

00:00:41.411 --> 00:00:43.909
Clue. Predict. Match.

00:00:45.109 --> 00:00:45.926
Clue rules

00:00:46.326 --> 00:00:48.388
Contrast clues flip the meaning

00:00:48.668 --> 00:00:50.181
although, but, while, yet

00:00:50.461 --> 00:00:54.223
Right: Although the trail looked easy, it was strenuous.

00:00:54.773 --> 00:00:56.636
Restatement clues repeat it

00:00:56.916 --> 00:00:59.306
a colon, a dash, “that is”

00:00:59.586 --> 00:01:03.442
Right: She was considerate: she listened to everyone.

00:01:03.992 --> 00:01:05.650
Match the tone and strength

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:08.455
“Not a compliment” needs a negative word.

00:01:09.005 --> 00:01:10.569
Beware the common meaning

00:01:10.849 --> 00:01:14.290
“Qualified” can mean “limited”, not “certified”.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:16.551
Let’s try one

00:01:16.951 --> 00:01:22.269
Although the scientist’s early experiments were ______, producing results that differed every time

00:01:22.269 --> 00:01:28.482
she repeated them, her later work was remarkably consistent and became a foundation for the field.

00:01:29.132 --> 00:01:34.406
Although sets up a contrast with her later work, which was remarkably consistent.

00:01:34.956 --> 00:01:38.762
And right after the blank: results that differed every time.

00:01:38.762 --> 00:01:41.937
So predict a simple word: unreliable.

00:01:42.487 --> 00:01:45.753
Influential, inexpensive, meticulous:

00:01:45.753 --> 00:01:49.775
none of them mean unreliable. Inconsistent does.

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:50.486
Choice A.

00:01:51.686 --> 00:01:52.755
Common traps

00:01:53.156 --> 00:01:54.263
The common meaning

00:01:54.543 --> 00:01:57.255
The obvious definition is often the trap.

00:01:57.805 --> 00:01:58.910
The topic word

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:02.244
Sounds related. Doesn’t fit the logic.

00:02:03.444 --> 00:02:04.923
Words in Context

00:02:05.203 --> 00:02:07.700
Clue. Predict. Match.

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:08.830
Spot it

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:12.101
Blank or underlined word + 4 single words

00:02:12.651 --> 00:02:13.358
Steps

00:02:13.558 --> 00:02:15.218
1. Read the whole passage

00:02:15.498 --> 00:02:16.700
2. Find the clue

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.116
3. Predict your own simple word

00:02:19.396 --> 00:02:21.725
4. Match meaning, direction, strength

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:22.999
Remember

00:02:23.199 --> 00:02:25.503
although / but / while → opposite meaning

00:02:25.783 --> 00:02:28.030
colon / dash / that is → same idea

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:31.217
Match the tone: positive or negative

00:02:31.497 --> 00:02:34.616
Underlined word: beware the common meaning

00:02:35.166 --> 00:02:35.607
Trap

00:02:35.807 --> 00:02:38.328
The topic word that only sounds related

00:02:39.078 --> 00:02:42.496
